Flex-Grow property of CSS flexbox layout allow us to define the size of the flexbox items in comparison to its siblings. We define the flex-grow sizing to the 
sibling items in a proportion or ratio using a value greater than 0. This distributes the empty space among the siblings as per the proprtion assigned to them.

.item-a{
  flex-grow: 1;
}

.item-b{
  flex-grow: 3;
}

Item-a will take 1 portion and item-b will take 3 portion of the remaining space and this will be added to their initial length.
